In addition to the reasons set forth in section 78-43, the city also reserves the right to discontinue service to a consumer for the following reasons:
(1) To prevent fraud or abuse;
(2) Consumer's willful disregard of the city's rules and regulations, and ordinances;
(3) Emergency repairs;
(4) Insufficiency of water supply due to circumstances beyond the control of the city;
(5) Legal processes;
(6) Direction of public authorities; or
(7) Strike, riot, fire, flood or unavoidable accident.
(Ord. No. 91-3, § 21-29, 6-10-1991)
